  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 17,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.258,
            0.858,
            0.821,
            0.878
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note: The colours have been added to show the rotations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.064,
            0.378,
            0.081
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.194,
            0.12,
            0.877,
            0.142
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can it be done by changing the angles between the dotted lines?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.143,
            0.885,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If a figure with three radial arms should have rotational symmetry, then a rotated version of it should overlap with the original. Here are rough diagrams of both of them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.212,
            0.884,
            0.256
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If these two figures must overlap, what can you tell about the angles?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.274,
            0.757,
            0.421
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.306,
                0.274,
                0.757,
                0.421
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_17_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.446,
            0.884,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observe that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { A }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " must overlap "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{B}; \\angle \\mathrm{B}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " must overlap "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " must overlap "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { A }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.194,
            0.491,
            0.651,
            0.512
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A} = \\angle \\mathrm{B} = \\angle \\mathrm{C},"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " What must this angle be?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.512,
            0.884,
            0.563
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know that a full turn has 360 degrees. This is equally distributed amongst these three angles. So each angle must be "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{360^{\\circ}}{3} = 120^{\\circ}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.563,
            0.885,
            0.63
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the radial arms figure with 3 arms shows rotational symmetry when the angle between the adjacent dotted lines is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 2 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Use paper cutouts to verify this observation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.631,
            0.884,
            0.675
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now how many angles of rotation does the figure have and what are they?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.69,
            0.883,
            0.854
          ],
